    "## 🎯 Interview Questions & Answers\n",
    "\n",
    "### Q1. Types of Missing Data (MCAR, MAR, MNAR)?\n",
    "- **MCAR** (Missing Completely At Random): No pattern\n",
    "  - Example: Random survey skips\n",
    "- **MAR** (Missing At Random): Depends on other column\n",
    "  - Example: Age missing based on gender\n",
    "- **MNAR** (Missing Not At Random): Has a reason\n",
    "  - Example: Rich people hide income\n",
    "\n",
    "### Q2. When to Drop rows vs Impute?\n",
    "- **Drop** when: more than 40-50% data is missing\n",
    "  - Example: Cabin column in Titanic (77% missing)\n",
    "- **Impute** when: less than 30% missing\n",
    "  - Example: Age column (20% missing) → fill with median\n",
    "\n",
    "### Q3. How do outliers affect imputation?\n",
    "- Outliers pull the **Mean** away from center\n",
    "- Example: Fare=500 makes mean too high\n",
    "- Solution: Use **Median** instead of Mean\n",
    "- Median is not affected by extreme values\n",
    "\n",
    "### Q4. Mean vs Median Imputation?\n",
    "- **Mean:** Average of all values\n",
    "  - Use when: data is normally distributed\n",
    "  - Problem: Affected by outliers\n",
    "- **Median:** Middle value\n",
    "  - Use when: data has outliers\n",
    "  - Better for skewed data like Fare, Age\n",
    "\n",
    "### Q5. Role of Data Cleaning in ML Pipeline?\n",
    "- Garbage in = Garbage out\n",
    "- Clean data → Better model accuracy\n",
    "- Steps: Remove nulls → Fix outliers → \n",
    "  Encode categories → Scale features → Train model"
   ]
